# Written fresh for D:\Dev\momentum (M001 §2). Not carried from momentum-harness.
#
# EVERY RULE HERE IS ANCHORED with a leading slash unless it genuinely must match
# at any depth. The old repo's rules were unanchored -- `*.jsonl`, `*.zst` and
# `*.parquet` matched at any depth and would silently swallow a provenance
# companion or a ledger, so a file looked committed right up until the day
# someone went looking for it. That trap needed a negation block and a test to
# undo. Anchoring is the fix that does not need undoing.

# Claude Code config. ONE EXCEPTION, and it is as narrow as git allows.
#
# M001 §6 says "Do not copy .claude/ in any form", and the old tree's
# .claude/settings.local.json held a live Databento key. THAT RULE STANDS for
# everything below except four .md files.
#
# 024 puts the subagent roster in `.claude/agents/` because CLAUDE CODE READS
# AGENT DEFINITIONS FROM THAT PATH AND NOWHERE ELSE -- the location is forced by
# the tool, not chosen. The roster's whole point is that a reviewer with no Edit
# tool cannot edit, and a restriction that is not committed is a restriction the
# next clone does not have.
#
#   .claude/*             ignore everything at the top level...
#   !.claude/agents/      ...except the agents DIRECTORY, so git descends into it
#   .claude/agents/*      ignore everything inside it...
#   !.claude/agents/*.md  ...except the definitions themselves
#
# THE DIRECTORY FORM `.claude/` WOULD HAVE MADE THIS IMPOSSIBLE, and that is why
# it is gone: git does not descend into an ignored directory, so no negation
# inside one can rescue anything.
#
# NOTHING ELSE BECOMES TRACKABLE. Not settings.local.json, not a .json at any
# depth under agents/, not a subdirectory under agents/, not worktrees/.
# `.claude/**/*.json` is belt-and-braces -- later rules win in git, so a future
# edit that widens the exception still cannot admit a JSON config without
# deleting a line that says why it exists.
#
# 046 ADDS ONE MORE EXCEPTION, and it is one exact filename.
#
#   !.claude/settings.json   the SHARED permission policy
#
# It sits AFTER the blanket rule because that is the only position git will
# honour, and it names a single path rather than a pattern. **What it does not
# admit is the point**: `settings.local.json` -- the shape that held a live
# Databento key in the predecessor tree -- is still ignored, and so is every
# other .json at every depth. A permission policy that is not committed is a
# policy the next clone does not have, which is the same argument that opened
# the agents/ exception under 024.
#
# THE ORDER OF THE LAST TWO LINES IS LOAD-BEARING and is asserted, not just
# written here: the blanket rule must stay directly above, so a widened negation
# added after it still goes red. See
# tests/test_claude_dir_stays_ignored.py::test_a_json_under_agents_is_ignored_even_if_the_negation_widens
#
# tests/test_claude_dir_stays_ignored.py asserts every one of these with
# `git check-ignore`, and was seen RED against a planted
# .claude/agents/settings.local.json before it was accepted.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/*.md
.claude/**/*.json
!.claude/settings.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Credentials never live in the tree - read them from the environment.
# tests/test_no_secrets.py enforces this; these lines are the first defence.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets.yaml

# Market data is large and licensed - never commit it. Anchored: a file named
# `notes.zst` inside an evidence folder is not market data.
/raw/
/bars/
/cache/
/selection/
*.dbn
*.dbn.zst

# Local append-only run state, carried as evidence but not tracked. The payloads
# are large and regenerable-in-shape; the LEDGERS are not, and those are tracked
# (see EVIDENCE-CARRY.md).
/records/
/records_truncated/

# The adoption drop folder lives outside both repos (D:\Dev\_adopt\) and is
# never committed. This line is belt-and-braces in case one is made in-tree.
/_adopt/

# verify.ps1's output (023). GENERATED, PER-MACHINE, AND DESCRIBES A MOMENT.
# Committing it would create a second source of truth about the tree that ages
# badly and diffs noisily on every run. Anchored: only the repo root.
# tests/test_verify_output_is_ignored.py asserts this with `git check-ignore`.
/handoff/verify-output.md
# The two RETIRED locations, kept ignored on purpose (054 Part 4). Extension
# changed .txt -> .md so the artifact is inside export-handoff.ps1's .md-only
# filter; before that it was inside handoff/verify-output.txt (053 Part 2),
# before that the repository root (through 023). A stale copy at either old
# path on any machine that ran an earlier verify.ps1 must not present itself
# to git as new work, and two files claiming to be THE verification record is
# the byte-indistinguishable defect in a new place.
/handoff/verify-output.txt
# The RETIRED location, kept ignored on purpose. 053 Part 2 moved the file into
# handoff/ so the export could carry it. A stale artifact from before that move
# still sits at the root on any machine that ran verify.ps1 earlier, and without
# this line it stops being ignored and presents itself to git as new work.
/verify-output.txt

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# 045 Part 3. Derived from the tree by tools/now.py on every verify.ps1 run.
# Tracked would mean a dirty tree after every run and three sessions colliding
# on a file whose whole content is recomputable.
claude/NOW.md

# 068 Part A. verify.ps1's second exemption to writing nothing but its own
# output file: the previous run's named-failure set, so section 1 can report
# a delta instead of a note having to quote a count. Generated, per-machine,
# describes a moment — same reasoning as /handoff/verify-output.md above.
# Anchored: only the repo root, which is the one place verify.ps1 writes it.
/verify-failures.txt
